1-2|1 Beggar, thief, or urchin: Player-character is bumped accidentally by a beggar, thief, or urchin.
3-5|[[1d4]] Beggars, thieves, or urchins: Beggar, thief, or urchin is begging. If no money is given, roll [[1d6]]: on a result of 1-2, he attempts to trip a player-character; on a result of 3-6, he insults a player-character.
6-9|[[1d4]] (plus [[1]] lurking nearby) Beggars, thieves, or urchins: Beggar, thief, or urchin bumps and attempts to rob player-character.
10-11|1 Beggar or thief (plus [[1]] lurking nearby): Beggar, thief tries to lure player-characters into an alley to be mugged by [[1d10]] accomplices.
12-15|1 Beggar, thief, or urchin: Beggar, thief, or urchin tries to con the player-characters; roll [[1d20]]+1 on the encounter matrix list for the disguise of the con-man; re-roll on a result of 10.
16-17|[[1d4]] Beggars or thieves: Beggar, thief is in trouble with the Thieves Guild and needs help.
18-19|[[2d6]] Beggars or thieves: Beggar, thief wants to hire player-characters for a mission: see Table 29 to define the mission.
20|1 Beggar or thief: Beggar, thief recognizes player-character. Roll [[1d20]]: on a result of 1-12, he is mistaken; on 13-20, he is correct.